135:// and `before`/`after` become `ReadonlyArray<{ index: number; message: Message }>`
155:- Order is DFS, parents before children, children in creation order. A child's opening is reflected on after the parent turn that spawned it, so the graph is built in the order the user actually learned.
174:  - Every emitted block carries the index it sits at in its thread's `messages`, including the `before`/`after` context, so an address rendered into a prompt round-trips back to the same block.
191:  - `reflectPrompt` renders the interaction's own address, and the addresses of its `before`/`after` blocks, and they resolve back to those blocks through `resolve`.
